From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 07:57:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AP: Keep the OBSS colours of a radio

hostapd kept the colours to avoid in color_collision_bitmap of a BSS.
Each collision event of the kernel and each BSS Color Collision report
replaced the bitmap of the first BSS of the radio. mac80211 repeats the
event at most every 500 ms with the colliding colour only
(ieee80211_rx_check_bss_color_collision()), so each event erased the
colours that stations reported. A BSS Color In Use report names no OBSS
colour: it names a colour that the station uses with a peer (IEEE Std
802.11-2024, 11.21.2.8), and a report of colour 0 cancels it.

Keep the OBSS colours per radio. A colour stays 60 s after a collision
event names it (dot11BSSColorCollisionAPPeriod plus the 10 s margin of
hostapd_switch_color()). It stays 130 s after a report names it (the
maximum dot11BSSColorCollisionSTAPeriod of 120 s plus the same margin).
The ageing pauses while BSS Color is disabled, since stations then stop
their reports (26.17.3.5.2) and mac80211 checks for no collision. Keep
the colour of a BSS Color In Use report per station, until the station
cancels it or leaves. A colour change avoids the colours of both sets.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
